      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-2-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Rules applicable to Australian citizens under the old Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-2-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to a person who was an Australian citizen under the\nAustralian Citizenship Act 1948 immediately before the commencement\nday.\nNote:\nThe person becomes an Australian citizen under the new Act: see subsection 4(1) of the\nnew Act.\nSame kind of citizenship\n(2)\nIf the person, immediately before the commencement day, was an\nAustralian citizen under the provision set out in column 2 of the\nfollowing table, the person is taken, on and from that day, to be an\nAustralian citizen under the provision set out in column 3 of the table:\n\nSame kind of citizenship\nColumn 1\nItem\nColumn 2\nProvision under which person was\na citizen\nColumn 3\nProvision under which person\nis taken to be a citizen\nSection 10B, 10C or 11 of the old\nAct\nSubdivision A of Division 2 of\nPart 2 of the new Act\nDivision 2 of Part III of the old Act\nSubdivision B of Division 2 of\nPart 2 of the new Act\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383\n\nSchedule 3  Application and transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThis item applies to a person who was an Australian citizen under the\nAustralian Citizenship Act 1948 immediately before the commencement\nday.\nNote:\nThe person becomes an Australian citizen under the new Act: see subsection 4(1) of the\nnew Act.\nSame kind of citizenship\n(2)\nIf the person, immediately before the commencement day, was an\nAustralian citizen under the provision set out in column 2 of the\nfollowing table, the person is taken, on and from that day, to be an\nAustralian citizen under the provision set out in column 3 of the table:\n\nSame kind of citizenship\nColumn 1\nItem\nColumn 2\nProvision under which person was\na citizen\nColumn 3\nProvision under which person\nis taken to be a citizen\nSection 10B, 10C or 11 of the old\nAct\nSubdivision A of Division 2 of\nPart 2 of the new Act\nDivision 2 of Part III of the old Act\nSubdivision B of Division 2 of\nPart 2 of the new Act\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383\n\nSchedule 3  Application and transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-2-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-2-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-2-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-2-3-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-2-3-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-2-3-logic-deontic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-2-3-logic-deontic-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b1850468799e4ccb2e49ebba2130d356d87425b5c3c76baa48b05b8d74d026ee",
      "skos:note": "Australian citizen under the old Act remains an Australian citizen under the new Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-2-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Rules applicable to Australian citizens under the old Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThis item applies to a person who was an Australian citizen under the\nAustralian Citizenship Act 1948 immediately before the commencement\nday.\nNote:\nThe person becomes an Australian citizen under the new Act: see subsection 4(1) of the\nnew Act.\nSame kind of citizenship\n(2)\nIf the person, immediately before the commencement day, was an\nAustralian citizen under the provision set out in column 2 of the\nfollowing table, the person is taken, on and from that day, to be an\nAustralian citizen under the provision set out in column 3 of the table:\n\nSame kind of citizenship\nColumn 1\nItem\nColumn 2\nProvision under which person was\na citizen\nColumn 3\nProvision under which person\nis taken to be a citizen\nSection 10B, 10C or 11 of the old\nAct\nSubdivision A of Division 2 of\nPart 2 of the new Act\nDivision 2 of Part III of the old Act\nSubdivision B of Division 2 of\nPart 2 of the new Act\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383\n\nSchedule 3  Application and transitional provisions"
    },
