    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-3-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Expanded meaning of some expressions in the new Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-3-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Unlawful non-citizen\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subparagraph 16(2)(b)(i), subsection 19C(3) and\nparagraphs 22(1)(b) and (6)(a) of the new Act, a person is taken to also\nhave been present in Australia as an unlawful non-citizen at a particular\ntime if the person:\n\n(a) in relation to the period beginning on 19 December 1989 and\nending on 31 August 1994—was an illegal entrant at that\ntime within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958 as in\nforce at that time; and\n\n(b) in relation to the period beginning on 2 April 1984 and\nending on 18 December 1989—was a prohibited non-citizen\nat that time within the meaning of that Act as in force at that\ntime; and\n\n(c) in relation to the period before 2 April 1984—was a\nprohibited immigrant at that time within the meaning of that\nAct as in force at that time; and\n\n(d) for any time—was in Australia at that time in contravention\nof a law of Norfolk Island or the Territory of Cocos\n(Keeling) Islands.\nPermanent visa\n(2)\nFor the purposes of the new Act, the definition of permanent visa in\nsection 3 of the new Act includes a valid permanent entry permit within\nthe meaning of the Migration Act 1958 as in force immediately before",
      "skos:definition": "Unlawful non-citizen\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subparagraph 16(2)(b)(i), subsection 19C(3) and\nparagraphs 22(1)(b) and (6)(a) of the new Act, a person is taken to also\nhave been present in Australia as an unlawful non-citizen at a particular\ntime if the person:\n\n(a) in relation to the period beginning on 19 December 1989 and\nending on 31 August 1994—was an illegal entrant at that\ntime within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958 as in\nforce at that time; and\n\n(b) in relation to the period beginning on 2 April 1984 and\nending on 18 December 1989—was a prohibited non-citizen\nat that time within the meaning of that Act as in force at that\ntime; and\n\n(c) in relation to the period before 2 April 1984—was a\nprohibited immigrant at that time within the meaning of that\nAct as in force at that time; and\n\n(d) for any time—was in Australia at that time in contravention\nof a law of Norfolk Island or the Territory of Cocos\n(Keeling) Islands.\nPermanent visa\n(2)\nFor the purposes of the new Act, the definition of permanent visa in\nsection 3 of the new Act includes a valid permanent entry permit within\nthe meaning of the Migration Act 1958 as in force immediately before",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-3-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-3-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-3-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-3-2-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-3-2-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-3-2-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0b214616c8c494a26cc5613aeb299d33322b3efd1f04ba9c19a70b9b729c76cc",
      "skos:note": "A person is taken to have been an unlawful non-citizen if they meet certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-3-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Expanded meaning of some expressions in the new Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Unlawful non-citizen\n(1)\nFor the purposes of subparagraph 16(2)(b)(i), subsection 19C(3) and\nparagraphs 22(1)(b) and (6)(a) of the new Act, a person is taken to also\nhave been present in Australia as an unlawful non-citizen at a particular\ntime if the person:\n\n(a) in relation to the period beginning on 19 December 1989 and\nending on 31 August 1994—was an illegal entrant at that\ntime within the meaning of the Migration Act 1958 as in\nforce at that time; and\n\n(b) in relation to the period beginning on 2 April 1984 and\nending on 18 December 1989—was a prohibited non-citizen\nat that time within the meaning of that Act as in force at that\ntime; and\n\n(c) in relation to the period before 2 April 1984—was a\nprohibited immigrant at that time within the meaning of that\nAct as in force at that time; and\n\n(d) for any time—was in Australia at that time in contravention\nof a law of Norfolk Island or the Territory of Cocos\n(Keeling) Islands.\nPermanent visa\n(2)\nFor the purposes of the new Act, the definition of permanent visa in\nsection 3 of the new Act includes a valid permanent entry permit within\nthe meaning of the Migration Act 1958 as in force immediately before"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-3-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
