      "cml:integrityHash": "1ddd2202c2370b3ce01e06224acb200acdc9a80dd0751b9375ff564187b4065e",
      "skos:note": "Citizenship by birth under the new Act applies to persons born on or after the commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Citizenship by birth under the new Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nParagraph 12(1)(a) of the new Act applies to a person born on or after\nthe commencement day.\n(2)\nParagraph 12(1)(b) of the new Act applies to:\n\n(a) a person born on or after the commencement day; and\n\n(b) a person born before the commencement day who,\nimmediately before that day, has not been ordinarily resident\nin Australia throughout the period of 10 years beginning on\nthe day the person was born.\nNote:\nThe effect of paragraph (b) of subitem (2) is that the period for which the person has\nbeen ordinarily resident in Australia before the commencement day will be counted\nunder the new Act."
    },
