        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d6b8f8118b723bc503fbdf93375e74d389756bec06fe15d282b485e584c200ce",
      "skos:note": "Section 19C of the new Act applies to adoptions that occur before, on or after the commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-5a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5A Citizenship for persons adopted in accordance with the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "Hague Convention on Intercountry Adoption\n(1)\nSection 19C of the new Act applies in relation to adoptions that occur\nbefore, on or after the commencement day.\n(2)\nParagraphs 19C(2)(e) and (f) of the new Act apply as if a reference to\nSubdivision A included a reference to section 10B, 10C or 11 of the old\nAct (about citizenship by descent)."
    },
