      "cml:integrityHash": "6b9adf1f1cbcf6db1c7eb1a8c5f72ccfa158e76431756edc2e3b745beb655898",
      "skos:note": "Minister cannot take into account certain periods when determining citizenship."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-5b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5B(3) Citizenship by conferral—persons who are permanent",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of subsection (1), the Minister must not take into\naccount any period during which the person has been:\n\n(a) confined in a prison; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383\n\nApplication and transitional provisions  Schedule 3\nProvisions relating to the enactment of the Australian Citizenship Act 2007  Part 1\n\nAustralian Citizenship (Transitionals and Consequentials) Act 2007\nCompilation date: 1/7/15\nRegistered: 10/8/15\n\n(b) confined in a psychiatric institution by order of a court made\nin connection with proceedings for an offence against an\nAustralian law in relation to the person.\n(3)\nIn applying section 22 of the new Act to an application covered by\nsubitem (1), subsections 22(5), (6) and (11) of the new Act have effect\nas if the reference in those subsections to “paragraph (1)(c)” were a\nreference to “subsection (1)” (as applied by subitem (2) of this item)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-5b-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
