    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Person granted certificate of citizenship under the old Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "but not an Australian citizen under the old Act\n(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has been granted a certificate of Australian\ncitizenship under section 13 of the old Act before the\ncommencement day; and\n\n(b) the certificate is in force immediately before that day; and\n\n(c) the person has not become an Australian citizen under\nsection 15 of the old Act immediately before that day;\nthe certificate is, on and from the commencement day, taken to be an\napproval given to the person under section 24 of the new Act.\nCancellation of approval under the new Act\n(2)\nFor the purposes of applying section 25 of the new Act to such an\napproval:\n\n(a) if the person was granted the certificate of Australian\ncitizenship under subsection 13(1) of the old Act—\nparagraph 25(2)(a) of the new Act is taken to apply to the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the reference in paragraph 25(3)(a) of the new Act to the day\non which the person received notice of the approval is taken\nto be a reference to the day on which the person was notified\nof the Minister’s decision under section 13 of the old Act to\ngrant the certificate.\nDeferral of pledge of commitment under old Act\n(3)\nIf a decision is in force under subsection 14C(1) of the old Act\nimmediately before the commencement day, the decision is, on and\nfrom the commencement day, taken to be a determination made under\nsubsection 26(3) of the new Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383\n\nSchedule 3  Application and transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "but not an Australian citizen under the old Act\n(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has been granted a certificate of Australian\ncitizenship under section 13 of the old Act before the\ncommencement day; and\n\n(b) the certificate is in force immediately before that day; and\n\n(c) the person has not become an Australian citizen under\nsection 15 of the old Act immediately before that day;\nthe certificate is, on and from the commencement day, taken to be an\napproval given to the person under section 24 of the new Act.\nCancellation of approval under the new Act\n(2)\nFor the purposes of applying section 25 of the new Act to such an\napproval:\n\n(a) if the person was granted the certificate of Australian\ncitizenship under subsection 13(1) of the old Act—\nparagraph 25(2)(a) of the new Act is taken to apply to the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the reference in paragraph 25(3)(a) of the new Act to the day\non which the person received notice of the approval is taken\nto be a reference to the day on which the person was notified\nof the Minister’s decision under section 13 of the old Act to\ngrant the certificate.\nDeferral of pledge of commitment under old Act\n(3)\nIf a decision is in force under subsection 14C(1) of the old Act\nimmediately before the commencement day, the decision is, on and\nfrom the commencement day, taken to be a determination made under\nsubsection 26(3) of the new Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383\n\nSchedule 3  Application and transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c089512e3ddbb0150b2a03972d6b960c5e2619c16ca17385417be82aeddec6e9",
      "skos:note": "Certificate of citizenship under old Act remains valid after commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007#sch-3-sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Person granted certificate of citizenship under the old Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "but not an Australian citizen under the old Act\n(1)\nIf:\n\n(a) a person has been granted a certificate of Australian\ncitizenship under section 13 of the old Act before the\ncommencement day; and\n\n(b) the certificate is in force immediately before that day; and\n\n(c) the person has not become an Australian citizen under\nsection 15 of the old Act immediately before that day;\nthe certificate is, on and from the commencement day, taken to be an\napproval given to the person under section 24 of the new Act.\nCancellation of approval under the new Act\n(2)\nFor the purposes of applying section 25 of the new Act to such an\napproval:\n\n(a) if the person was granted the certificate of Australian\ncitizenship under subsection 13(1) of the old Act—\nparagraph 25(2)(a) of the new Act is taken to apply to the\nperson; and\n\n(b) the reference in paragraph 25(3)(a) of the new Act to the day\non which the person received notice of the approval is taken\nto be a reference to the day on which the person was notified\nof the Minister’s decision under section 13 of the old Act to\ngrant the certificate.\nDeferral of pledge of commitment under old Act\n(3)\nIf a decision is in force under subsection 14C(1) of the old Act\nimmediately before the commencement day, the decision is, on and\nfrom the commencement day, taken to be a determination made under\nsubsection 26(3) of the new Act.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015C00383\n\nSchedule 3  Application and transitional provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-8-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-transitionals-and-consequentials-act-2007-sch-3-sec-8"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
